{
  "title": "55: al-Rahmaan الرحمن",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَلرَّحْمٰنُۙ‏(1)\nAR-RAHMAAN.\n(God) The Beneficent\nعَلَّمَ الْقُرْاٰنَؕ‏(2)\nA’LLAMAL QURAAN.\nTaught He the Qur’an\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَۙ‏(3)\nKHALAQAL INSAAN.\nHe created man\nعَلَّمَهُ الْبَيَانَ‏(4)\nA’LLAMAHUL BAYAAN.\nHe taught him expression\nاَلشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ بِحُسْبَانٍ‏(5)\nASH-SHAMSO WAL-QAMARO BE HUSBAANIN.\nThe sun and the moon follow the (prescribed) timings\nوَّالنَّجْمُ وَالشَّجَرُ يَسْجُدٰنِ‏(6)\nWAN-NAJMO WASH-SHAJARO YASJODAAN.\nAnd the herbs and the trees do obeisance (unto Him)\nوَالسَّمَآءَ رَفَعَهَا وَوَضَعَ الْمِيْزَانَۙ‏(7)\nWAS-SAMAAA-A RAFA-A’HAA WA-WAZA-A’L MEEZAAN.\nAnd the heaven, He did raise it high, and placed the scale (within reach)\nاَلَّا تَطْغَوْا فِى الْمِيْزَانِ‏(8)\nALLAA TATGHAW FIL MEEZAAN.\nSo that ye may not transgress in scales\nوَاَقِيْمُوا الْوَزْنَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَلَا تُخْسِرُوا الْمِيْزَانَ‏(9)\nWA AQEEMUL WAZNA BIL QISTE WA LAA TUKHSERUL MEEZAAN.\nAnd maintain ye the measure with justice and do not cut short in the scale\nوَالْاَرْضَ وَضَعَهَا لِلْاَنَامِۙ‏(10)\nWAL ARZA WA ZA-A’HAA LIL ANAAM.\nAnd the earth, He hath made it for (His) (living) creatures\nفِيْهَا فَاكِهَةٌ  ۙ وَّالنَّخْلُ ذَاتُ الْاَكْمَامِ ۖ‏(11)\nFEEHAA FAAKEHATUNW WAN-NAKHLO ZAATUL AKMAAM.\nTherein is fruit and palms having, sheathed clusters\nوَالْحَبُّ ذُو الْعَصْفِ وَالرَّيْحَانُۚ‏(12)\nWAL-HABBO ZUL-A’SFE WAR-RAYHAAN.\nAnd corn with (its) leaves and stalks and with sweet-smelling herbs\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(13)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two (men and jinns ) belie?\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ كَالْفَخَّارِۙ‏(14)\nKHALAQAL INSAANA MIN SALSAALIN KAL-FAKHKHAAR.\nHe created man from dry clay like that of the earthen vessels\nوَخَلَقَ الْجَآنَّ مِنْ مَّارِجٍ مِّنْ نَّارٍۚ‏(15)\nWA KHALAQAL JAAAN-NA MIN MAAREJIM MIN NAAR.\nAnd created He the jinn of a flame of fire\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(16)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nرَبُّ الْمَشْرِقَيْنِ وَ رَبُّ الْمَغْرِبَيْنِۚ‏(17)\nRABBUL MASHREQAYNE WA RABBUL MAGHREBAYN.\n(He alone is the) Lord of the two easts and the Lord of the two wests\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(18)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nمَرَجَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ يَلْتَقِيٰنِۙ‏(19)\nMARAJAL BAHRAYNE YALTAQEYAAN.\nHe hath let loose the two seas that they flow together meeting each other\nبَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخٌ لَّا يَبْغِيٰنِۚ‏(20)\nBAYNAHOMAA BARZAKHUL LAA YABGHEYAAN.\n(Yet) between them (He hath caused) a barrier, (that) they encroach not (one upon another)\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(21)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties your Lord will ye two belie?\nيَخْرُجُ مِنْهُمَا اللُّؤْلُؤُ وَالْمَرْجَانُۚ‏(22)\nYAKHROJO MINHOMAL LO-LO-O WAL MARJAAN.\nCome forth out of the two, pearls and corals\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(23)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nوَلَهُ الْجَوَارِ الْمُنْشَئٰتُ فِى الْبَحْرِ كَالْاَعْلَامِۚ‏(24)\nWA LAHUL JAWAARIL MUNSHA-AATO FIL BAHRE KAL-A-A’LAAM.\nAnd His are the ships towering up at the sea like mountains\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(25)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of vour Lord will ve two belie?\nكُلُّ مَنْ عَلَيْهَا فَانٍ ۚ ۖ‏(26)\nKULLO MAN A’LAYHAA FAANIN.\nEvery one on it shall perish\nوَّيَبْقٰى وَجْهُ رَبِّكَ ذُو الْجَلٰلِ وَالْاِكْرَامِۚ‏(27)\nWA YABQAA WAJHO RABBEKA ZUL-JALAALE WAL-IKRAAM.\nBut will remain for ever the Face of thy Lord, the Glorious and Gracious\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(28)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of thy Lord will ye two belie?\nيَسْئَلُهٗ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ كُلَّ يَوْمٍ هُوَ فِىْ شَاْنٍۚ‏(29)\nYAS-ALOHU MAN FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZ, KULLA YAWMIN HOWA FEE SHAAN.\nBeseech Him all those in the heavens and the earth; Every day He is in a (new) splendorous manifestation\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(30)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nسَنَفْرُغُ لَكُمْ اَيُّهَ الثَّقَلٰنِۚ‏(31)\nSANAFROGHO LAKUM AYYOHAS SAQALAAN.\nSoon will We attend to you, O’ ye two groups (of men and jinns)\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(32)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nيٰمَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ اِنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ اَنْ تَنْفُذُوْا مِنْ اَقْطَارِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ فَانْفُذُوْاؕ لَا تَنْفُذُوْنَ اِلَّا بِسُلْطٰنٍۚ‏(33)\nYAA MA’SHARAL JINNE WAL INSE ENIS TA-TA’TUM AN TANFOZOO MIN AQTAARIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE FANFOZOO, LAA TANFOZOONA ILLAA BE SULTAAN.\nO ye peoples of jinn and humans, if ye can penetrate the bounds of the heavens and the earth, then do penetrate ye through; (But) ye cannot penetrate but with (Our) authority!\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(34)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nيُرْسَلُ عَلَيْكُمَا شُوَاظٌ مِّنْ نَّارٍ ۙ وَّنُحَاسٌ فَلَا تَنْتَصِرٰنِۚ‏(35)\nYURSALO A’LAYKOMAA SHOWAAZUM MIN NAARINW, WA NOHAASUN FALAA TANTASERAAN.\nOn ye two shall be sent the flames of fire and molten brass, then ye shall not be able to protect yourselves\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(36)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفَاِذَا انْشَقَّتِ السَّمَآءُ فَكَانَتْ وَرْدَةً كَالدِّهَانِۚ‏(37)\nFA-EZAN SHAQQATIS SAMAAA-O FA-KAANAT WARDATAN KAD-DEHAAN.\nAnd when is rent asunder the heaven, then it becometh red like the tanned hide\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(38)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفَيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا يُسْئَلُ عَنْ ذَنْۢبِهٖۤ اِنْسٌ وَّلَا جَآنٌّۚ‏(39)\nFA YAWMA-EZIL LAA YUS-ALO A’N ZANBEHI INSUNW WA LAA JAAAN.\nAnd on that Day shall not be asked man nor jinn of his sin\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(40)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nيُعْرَفُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ بِسِيْمٰهُمْ فَيُؤْخَذُ بِالنَّوَاصِىْ وَ الْاَقْدَامِۚ‏(41)\nYO’RAFUL MUJREMOONA BE SEEMAAHUM FA-YOO-KHAZO BIN NAWAASEE WAL AQDAAM.\nThe guilty ones shall be re-cognised by their marks, and they shall be seized by their forelocks and their feet\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(42)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nهٰذِهٖ جَهَنَّمُ الَّتِىْ يُكَذِّبُ بِهَا الْمُجْرِمُوْنَۘ‏(43)\nHAAZEHI JAHANNAMUL LATEE YOKAZZEBO BEHAL MUJREMOON.\nThis is the hell which belied the guilty ones\nيَطُوْفُوْنَ بَيْنَهَا وَبَيْنَ حَمِيْمٍ اٰنٍۚ‏(44)\nYATOOFOONA BAYNAHAA WA BAYNA HAMEEMIN AAN.\nAround in it shall they run in hot, boiling water\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(45)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nوَلِمَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهٖ جَنَّتٰنِۚ‏(46)\nWA LEMAN KHAAFA MAQAAMA RABBEHI JANNATAAN.\nAnd for him who feareth the time of standing before his Lord are two gardens\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۙ‏(47)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nذَوَاتَاۤ اَفْنَانٍۚ‏(48)\nZAWAATAA AFNAAN.\nWith over-branching trees (in each of the two gardens)\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(49)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفِيْهِمَا عَيْنٰنِ تَجْرِيٰنِۚ‏(50)\nFEEHEMAA A’YNAANE TAJREYAAN.\nIn both of them are two fountains flowing\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(51)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAANE.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفِيْهِمَا مِنْ كُلِّ فَاكِهَةٍ زَوْجٰنِۚ‏(52)\nFEEHEMAA MIN KULLE FAAKEHATIN ZAWJAAN.\nIn each of them, of every fruit, are two kinds\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(53)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلٰى فُرُشٍۢ بَطَآئِنُهَا مِنْ اِسْتَبْرَقٍؕ وَجَنَی الْجَنَّتَيْنِ دَانٍۚ‏(54)\nMUTTAKE-EENA A’LAA FOROSHIM BATAAA-ENOHAA MIN ISTABRAQIN, WA JANAL JANNATAYNE DAAN.\nReclining on beds, the inner coverings of which are of silk brocade; the fruit of (both) the gardens shall be nigh (within easy reach)\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(55)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفِيْهِنَّ قٰصِرٰتُ الطَّرْفِۙ لَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ اِنْسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَآنٌّۚ‏(56)\nFEEHINNA QAASERAATUT TARFE, LAM YATMISHUNNA INSUN QABLAHUM WALAA JAAAN.\nTherein shall be damsels with retiring glances, whom hath touched not ever before, any human being nor a jinn\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ ۚ‏(57)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nكَاَنَّهُنَّ الْيَاقُوْتُ وَالْمَرْجَانُۚ‏(58)\nKA-ANNAHUNNAL YAAQOOTO WAL MARJAAN.\nAs though they were rubies and pearls\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(59)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nهَلْ جَزَآءُ الْاِحْسَانِ اِلَّا الْاِحْسَانُۚ‏(60)\nHAL JAZAAA-UL EHSAANE ILLAL EHSAAN.\nIs the recompense for good aught but good?\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(61)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nوَمِنْ دُوْنِهِمَا جَنَّتٰنِۚ‏(62)\nWA MIN DOONEHEMAA JANNATAAN.\nAnd besides these (two) are two other gardens\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۙ‏(63)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nمُدْهَآمَّتٰنِۚ‏(64)\nMUD-HAAMMATAAN.\nDark-green in colour (being plentifully watered)\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(65)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفِيْهِمَا عَيْنٰنِ نَضَّاخَتٰنِۚ‏(66)\nFEEHEMAA A’YNAANE NAZZAAKHATAAN.\nIn them both are two springs gushing forth\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(67)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفِيْهِمَا فَاكِهَةٌ وَّنَخْلٌ وَّرُمَّانٌۚ‏(68)\nFEEHEMAA FAAKEHATUNW WA NAKHLUNW WA RUMMAAN.\nIn them both are fruits and palms and pomegranates\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(69)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nفِيْهِنَّ خَيْرٰتٌ حِسَانٌۚ‏(70)\nFEEHINNA KHAYRAATUN HESAAN.\nIn them are virtuous women, beautiful ones\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(71)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nحُوْرٌ مَّقْصُوْرٰتٌ فِى الْخِيَامِۚ‏(72)\nHOORUM MAQSOORAATUN FIL KHEYAAM.\nFair ones, close-guarded, in pavilions\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(73)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nلَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ اِنْسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَآنٌّۚ‏(74)\nLAM YAT-MISHUNNA INSUN QABLAHUM WA LAA JAAAN.\nHath touched them not ever before any human being nor any jinn\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(75)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلٰى رَفْرَفٍ خُضْرٍ وَّعَبْقَرِىٍّ حِسَانٍۚ‏(76)\nMUTTAKE-EENA A’LAA RAFRAFIN KHUZRINW WA A’BQARIYYIN HESAAN.\nReclining on cushions green and carpets beautiful\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(77)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nWhich then of the bounties of your Lord will ye two belie?\nتَبٰرَكَ اسْمُ رَبِّكَ ذِى الْجَلٰلِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ‏(78)\nTABAARAKAS-MO RABBEKA ZIL JALAALE WAL IKRAAM.\nHallowed is the name of thy Lord, the Lord of Glory and Grace!",
  "merits": "This Surah has 78 verses and it is ‘Makki’. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that reciting this Surah on Friday after the dawn prayers carries great reward. Surah as-Rahman removes hypocrisy from one’s heart.\nOn the Day of Judgement, this Surah will come in the shape of a human being who will be handsome and will have a very nice scent. Allah (s.w.t.) will then tell him to point out those people who used to recite this Surah and he will name them. Then he will be allowed to beg pardon for those whom he names and Allah (s.w.t.) will pardon them.\nThe Imam (a.s.) also said that if a person dies after reciting this Surah, then is considered a martyr. Writing this Surah and keeping it makes all difficulties and problems vanish and also cures eye ailments. Writing it on the walls of a house keeps away all types of household pests. If recited at night, then Allah (s.w.t.) sends an angel to guard the reciter until he wakes up and if recited in the daytime then an angel guards him until sunset."
